LOGBOOK.md:154:- ANOMALY: Xcode's generated package scheme copied both library-style XCFramework module maps to one custom `Release/include/module.modulemap`, producing a deterministic multiple-producer error once the libssh2 and native-fixture graphs met. The Apple matrix now keeps Xcode's existing device/simulator/native checks and uses isolated dual-architecture SwiftPM builds with `-application-extension` for the macOS provider/harness; the stripped release harness check verifies libssh2's intentionally hidden local rekey symbol separately from exported HEV symbols.
LOGBOOK.md:202:- ROOT CAUSE: r4 settled `macos.provider` with **no keychain row and no file exception** because `/System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb:792-793` grants `/Library/Keychains` read/write to any process holding `com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension`. Every observation was taken on **macOS 26.5 (25F71)**. The binding generated-target floor is **macOS 15.0** (`.spec/platform-distribution.md`, ADR-016/3r0993). A base sandbox grant is a property of the **running system**, not of this contract — so the matrix asserted, for nine major releases it never read, something true only of the one it did. Verdict 08 F1.
LOGBOOK.md:203:- FINDING: the consequence is not a missing entitlement but an **inverted one**. This matrix is the source for generated entitlements *and* for the automated allowlist checks, so a file exception genuinely required at the floor would have been rejected as an **unreviewed relaxation** under rule X1 / assertion A10a — the gate rejecting the correct answer, on a supported OS.
LOGBOOK.md:259:- SCOPE: one board field on one element — `TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope`, revision label only, character delta **0**. `TASK-260715-3jloqy` needed no change and still passes P1. No element created, deleted, re-parented or re-linked. No portal mutation, no product source, spec file, or generated project touched.
