16-## 1. Authority, precedence, and non-goals
17-
18-This is the production field and ordering contract for one selected macOS SSH
19-profile. It carries an immutable, non-secret profile snapshot from the
20-containing app to the root packet-tunnel provider, resolves an opaque
21:credential reference inside the provider, verifies host identity before any
22:credential lookup or authentication request, and returns stable typed evidence
23-or errors.
24-
25-The accepted macOS transport decision `TASK-260728-7ii1xz` supersedes stale
26-macOS wording in this task, `.spec/security-privacy.md`, and the older M1
27-lifecycle contract:
28-
29-1. The logged-in host and root provider do not resolve one shared App Group
30-   container. macOS profile transport uses `providerConfiguration`; neither
31-   side reads or writes an App Group profile snapshot.
32:2. The macOS provider has no Keychain Sharing entitlement or Keychain access
33:   group. It uses the provider-owned system-domain file-based Keychain and a
34-   per-item `SecAccess` ACL constrained to the provider's designated code
35-   requirement.
36-3. The complete non-secret snapshot replaces the older macOS
37-   `configurationReferenceKey` payload that contained only an opaque profile
38-   identifier. The manager ownership marker and manager-contract marker from
--
45-   diagnostic commands remain read-only, and profile/trust mutation still does
46-   not occur through provider RPC.
47-
48-This contract does not select or fork an SSH engine. It consumes the accepted
49-libssh2 adapter. It does not define profile editor presentation, key import or
50:generation, trust-confirmation presentation, password authentication, routing,
51-multi-lane identity checks, `ProxyJump`, SFTP, agent forwarding, interactive or
52-arbitrary shell access, or iOS behavior.
