261:mapping each nonzero `privateKeyFormat` value to an exact representation,
262-algorithm, byte bounds, parser, and selected-adapter signer construction, the
263-v1 registry is empty and production seeding fails closed with
264:`credentialFormatRegistryUnavailable`. Implementations may build and test the
265-codec/vault with non-production fixtures, but cannot accept a production seed
266:by inventing a local format value.
267-
268:Provider message handling is serialized with credential-vault operations, not
269-with tunnel start. Every seed is an add under a newly allocated reference;
270:credential replacement never updates the item named by the currently published
271-snapshot. A duplicate reference is idempotent only when the protected record's
272:request ID, credential generation, format, and secret-payload digest all match;
273:otherwise it returns `credentialReferenceCollision` and changes nothing. The
274-response is a non-secret
275-`CredentialMutationResponseV1` of at most 4096 bytes containing version, kind,
276:request ID, `stored|idempotent` outcome, stored credential generation,
277-and a stable error code if applicable. It contains no key-derived or
278:passphrase-derived data.
279-
280-The provider may be launched to handle this message while the tunnel is not
281-started. This does not imply the system VPN is connected. Failure to deliver is
282-reported; the host retains its bounded staging item until an explicit retry or
283-user cancellation under the M4 lifecycle contract.
