285-Create and replacement use this copy-on-write sequence:
286-
287:1. Host allocates a new opaque reference, a newer logical credential
288:   generation, and a request ID; it does not alter the current profile.
289:2. Provider stores the new exact item and confirms its generation.
290:3. Host stages the new `(ref, generation)` in the §4 publication WAL, publishes
291-   and verifies the complete new snapshot, then commits the host record.
292-4. Only after verified publication does the host request revocation of the old
293-   reference. A pending revocation is surfaced using §11; it does not roll back
294:   the now-authoritative new credential.
295-
